A||||2||OverDrive||I need advice.||||5||
Z||000000||OverDrive||06-11-2001||10:56 AM||||Okay, I have a REALLY beat up 84' Convertible. One I get some new tires, do a little mechanical work it'll be fine.<BR>It needs A LOT of body work. <BR>But on to my question. I need a new interior. Any suggestions? The one I have right now is so shitty. As soon as I get my digi cam (a few weeks) I'll take some "Before" pictures for people to see. Then (hopefully) by the end of the summer some "After" pics.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>My other question is what kind of tires do I need? Are there any special requirements?<BR>Thanks a ton.||||reg||5
Z||000001||stimpy||06-11-2001||11:57 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by OverDrive:<BR><B> I need a new interior. Any suggestions? The one I have right now is so shitty.<BR></B><P>I'd suggest you keep an eye on the mall. Also post exactly what pieces you need and pick them up as you can afford them. There are lots of people on the forum who have all the parts you might need. Best bet is to clean everything up best you can and see what's salvegeable. Warped pieces can be repaired by glueing and clamping the vynil parts to the plastic underneath.<P><B>My other question is what kind of tires do I need? Are there any special requirements?<BR>Thanks a ton.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well, they should be round.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Seriously, don't cheap out on the tires. Do not get high mile warranty tires, as they are made of very hard compound rubber. You'll wind up breaking the back end loose around every turn, especially when the weather gets poor. Also don't waste your money on an aggressive "performance" tire. Most Fieros don't need V or Z rated tires, especially not 84s.  I recommend a "Touring" or a "Grand Touring" tire. I have Bridgestone Turanza H Revo tires on my GT. Excellent wet weather handling, very quiet tires. Kinda spendy though, but they have a 50,000 mile waranty.||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroLisa||06-11-2001||12:24 PM||||I've re-done 2 interiors thus far. In my coupe, I just switched it out with a car that had a bad motor and a good interior, so you can do that, with just swapping pieces from other cars. Lots of people have miscellaneous parts that they want to get rid of, I know I did when I started customizing my GT. <BR>The way I did my GT was by repainting and replacing as necessary. If your interior is just faded, dirty, and warped, you can repair instead of replace.  If you have any questions about repainting interiors, feel free to email me.<P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 violet pearl 4 speed GT: 17 in. rims, lowered, cold-air intake<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A>*<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>NC Tarheels Fieros Site</A><P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/lisa1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
